# BEAST System - SAIA (Sovereign Autonomous Intelligence Architecture)

`beast-system-saia` is the core workspace and engine driving the Sovereign Autonomous Digital Governance Platform. It automates public benefit distribution, streamlines intake and submission workflows, and manages secure, audit-ready infrastructure integrations.

## Platform Modules

- **Governance Engine (`apps/governance-engine`)**: Core decision engine executing autonomous policy rules and benefit distribution verification.
- **Submission Gateway (`apps/submission-gateway`)**: Ingestion service handling intake forms, automated validation, and cryptographic audit proofs.
- **Web Dashboard (`apps/web-dashboard`)**: Front-end portal for platform oversight, analytics, and operational tracking.
- **Smart Contracts (`packages/smart-contracts`)**: On-chain registries for verifiable audit trails and state proofs.
- **Infrastructure (`packages/infrastructure`)**: Cloud provisioning configs (Google Cloud Run, Cloud SQL PostgreSQL).

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- Node.js >= 20.x
- Docker & Docker Compose
- Google Cloud SDK / GCP Access

### Local Setup
```bash
# Clone repository
git clone [https://github.com/PAT333-UX/beast-system-saia.git](https://github.com/PAT333-UX/beast-system-saia.git)
cd beast-system-saia

# Install dependencies across workspaces
npm install

# Run local development services via Docker Compose
docker-compose up -d
